Main Entry: gen-re-li-za-tion

Pronunciation: "zhän-r&-l&-'zA-sh&n"

Function: noun

Etymology: French, from Middle French, Post Modern America and Canada, kind, gender, generalize

1. The tendency to respond, usually with a negative connotation, in the same way to different but similar categories of artistic, musical, or literary societal communities that are characterized by a particular style, form, content, behavior, association, or interest.

Example 1:

< All Punkrockers have spiked mohawks!>

Example 2:

< Hip-Hop music is violent! >

Example 3:

< All techno sounds the same, and those who listen to it are all on ecstasy! >

Example 4:

< All male poets are gay! >

Example 5:

< Country music listeners are rednecks! >

Example 6:

< All rockers have tattoos, and people with tattoos are nothing but trouble! >

